# MDEC frame decode vectors (MdecFrameTests).
# Input: the block stream of CASE frame1 in wve-block.vectors (MOVIES/INTRO.WVE,
# video chunk index 1, header frame number 1, 320x192, chunk offset 26432),
# run through WveBlockDecoder, then MdecFrameDecoder.DecodeDecoderOutput.
# Only derived numbers are stored here: code words, coefficients, sample values and
# SHA-256 hashes; no image data.
#
# How it was produced:
# - PLANES/PIXEL/BIGENDIAN/REF: the .NET port (MdecFrameDecoder) on INTRO.WVE.
#   Hashes are SHA-256 over the int32 little-endian arrays (Y 320x192, Cb/Cr 160x96,
#   ARGB 320x192 as 0xFFRRGGBB).
# - BLOCK: a separate Python model of jpsxdec MdecDecoder_int + PsxMdecIDCT_int
#   fed with the WveBlockDecoder output; its full Y/Cb/Cr plane hashes equal PLANES.
# - The .NET RGB output equals jpsxdec v2.1-beta "-q psx" PNG output bit for bit on
#   all 837 frames jpsxdec extracts from INTRO.WVE (mean abs error 0.0); against the
#   default "-q high" output (float IDCT + bicubic chroma) the mean error is 0.78
#   (0.616 / 0.525 / 0.451 for chunks 0 / 100 / 400).
# - BIGENDIAN: the same input read as big-endian words (bytes swapped) before the
#   block decoder; MDEC decoding stops with a run past index 63 after 11 blocks.
#
# Rows:
# SIZE <width> <height>
# PLANES <status> <blocksDecoded> <codesConsumed> <sha Y> <sha Cb> <sha Cr> <sha ARGB>
# PIXEL <x> <y> <rgb hex> <Y> <Cb> <Cr>
# BLOCK <blockIndex> <qscale> <dc> <codeCount> <nonZero> <lastZigZagIndex> <codes hex> <64 dequantised coefficients> <64 IDCT outputs>
#   (coefficients and IDCT outputs in matrix row-major order; codeCount includes the
#   qscale/DC word and the 0xFE00 end code)
# BIGENDIAN <status> <blocksDecoded> <codesConsumed> <sha ARGB>
# REF <videoChunkIndex> <frameNumber> <width> <height> <chunkOffset> <chunkSize> <sha Y> <sha Cb> <sha Cr> <sha ARGB>
#   (only checked when MOVIES/INTRO.WVE is available locally)
SIZE 320 192
PLANES Complete 1440 19210 150eda6e52ed1cf2d6d49d6d9af0c013aeeaa532167c751bf7edc646f9b48c83 669430c5bf92b3ea47cd85cfc4c68d04fbbb099b8d47b847147b2c67c31c7eb6 a47682149c8588e87c328cb04c5f334de3a0d92b6c05346a8a6ee4e1829b43e3 fbb0ffa199b1a5068ab2ca8765d8efbee5587e041cd57a41eda08354f9ca7c7d
